-- title:
--   Twisting by rZ changes the Čech Euler characteristic by rd
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes, let $\iota : Y \to X$ be a morphism and let $y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper. Let $I$ be ideal sheaf data on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ lies in some basic open $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\, f$ for an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ such that the ideal of $I$ on the affine basic open of $f$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor, and assume the comap $I.\mathrm{comap}\,\iota$ is invertible in the same sense. Let $d \in \mathbb{N}$, and assume that the closed immersion of the subscheme cut out by $I.\mathrm{comap}\,\iota$ followed by $y$ satisfies `IsFinite`, with `finrank` equal to $d$ at every point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$. Let $M$ be a module on $X$ which is invertible, i.e. every point has an open neighbourhood $U$ over which the pullback of $M$ along $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of modules; let $r \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $\mathcal{W}$ be a two-chart cover of $Y$, given by two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ and $U_0 \sqcap U_1$ affine. For a module $N$ on $Y$, write $\chi(N)$ for $\dim_k H^0 - \dim_k H^1$ of the two-term complex $\Gamma(N,U_0) \oplus \Gamma(N,U_1) \to \Gamma(N, U_0 \sqcap U_1)$, $(m_0,m_1) \mapsto m_1|_{U_0\sqcap U_1} - m_0|_{U_0 \sqcap U_1}$, the $k$-structure coming from $y$. Then, with $(I^r).\mathrm{invModule}$ the dual of the module attached to $I^r$, $$\chi\bigl(\iota^*((I^r)^{\vee} \otimes M)\bigr) = \chi(\iota^* M) + r\,d$$ as an identity of integers.
--
--   This is the additivity of the degree of a line bundle on a proper $k$-scheme under twisting by $r$ times an effective Cartier divisor $Z = V(I)$, read through the restriction of $Z$ to $Y$ (a closed subscheme finite over $k$ of constant rank $d$), and expressed as an Euler characteristic of the two-chart Čech complex of a fixed two-affine-open cover. It is used in the subsequent computations of Euler characteristics for products and iterated powers of invertible ideal sheaves, and thence in the multidegree identities for line bundles on the curves occurring later in the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_IsInvertible_eulerChar_sectionsOf_pullback_pow_invModule_tensor_eq_add_mul.lean

